{"id":"mahabharata-3-228","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":228,"title":"अष्टाविंशत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 228 · The Kauravas set out","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra hesitates, fearing a clash with the Pandavas, but Shakuni assures him they will not go near them. Permission given, Duryodhana sets out with a vast train of soldiers, women and townsfolk and camps near the Dvaita forest.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಘರ್ಷಣೆಯ ಭಯದಿಂದ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನು ಹಿಂಜರಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅವರ ಬಳಿ ಹೋಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಶಕುನಿ ಭರವಸೆ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅನುಮತಿ ಪಡೆದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಸೈನಿಕರು, ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರು, ಪುರಜನರ ದೊಡ್ಡ ಪರಿವಾರದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೊರಟು ದ್ವೈತವನದ ಬಳಿ ಬೀಡುಬಿಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पाण्डवों से टकराव के भय से धृतराष्ट्र हिचकते हैं, पर शकुनि आश्वासन देता है कि वे उनके पास नहीं जाएँगे। अनुमति मिलने पर दुर्योधन सैनिकों, स्त्रियों और पुरवासियों के विशाल दल के साथ निकलता है और द्वैतवन के पास डेरा डालता है।","te":"పాండవులతో ఘర్షణ భయంతో ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు సందేహిస్తాడు, వారి దగ్గరకు వెళ్లబోమని శకుని హామీ ఇస్తాడు. అనుమతి పొంది దుర్యోధనుడు సైనికులు, స్త్రీలు, పౌరుల పెద్ద పరివారంతో బయలుదేరి ద్వైతవనం దగ్గర విడిది చేస్తాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்களுடன் மோதல் நேருமோ என்று அஞ்சி த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் தயங்க, அவர்கள் அருகே செல்ல மாட்டோம் என்று ஶகுனி உறுதியளிக்கிறான். அனுமதி பெற்றுத் துரியோதனன் வீரர்கள், பெண்கள், நகர மக்களின் பெரும் கூட்டத்துடன் புறப்பட்டு த்வைத வனத்தருகே பாசறை அமைக்கிறான்.","ml":"ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രൻ പാണ്ഡവരുമായുള്ള ഏറ്റുമുട്ടലിനെ ഭയന്ന് മടിക്കുന്നു; എന്നാൽ അവരുടെ അടുത്തേക്ക് പോകില്ലെന്ന് ശകുനി ഉറപ്പു നൽകുന്നു. അനുമതി ലഭിച്ചപ്പോൾ, സൈനികരും സ്ത്രീകളും പട്ടണവാസികളുമടങ്ങുന്ന വലിയ പരിവാരത്തോടെ ദുര്യോധനൻ പുറപ്പെട്ട് ദ്വൈതവനത്തിനടുത്ത് പാളയമടിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.228; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"घोषयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Ghoshayatra Parva (The cattle expedition)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रं ततः सर्वे ददृशुर्जनमेजय ।\nपृष्ट्वा सुखमथो राज्ञः पृष्ट्वा राज्ञा च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then, Janamejaya, they all went to see Dhritarashtra, asking after the king's welfare and being asked in turn by him, descendant of Bharata.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"ततस्तैर्विहितः पूर्वं समङ्गो नाम बल्लवः ।\nसमीपस्थास्तदा गावो धृतराष्ट्रे न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then a cowherd named Samanga, previously instructed by them, informed Dhritarashtra that the cattle were nearby.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"अनन्तरं च राधेयः शकुनिश्च विशां पते ।\nआहतुः पार्थिवश्रेष्ठं धृतराष्ट्रं जनाधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"After that, lord of the people, Radheya and Shakuni spoke to Dhritarashtra, best of kings and ruler of men.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"रमणीयेषु देशेषु घोषाः संप्रति कौरव ।\nस्मारणासमयः प्राप्तो वत्सानामपि चाङ्कनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Kaurava, the cattle stations are now in delightful regions. The time has come for the counting and for branding the calves.'\""}},{"n":5,"text":"मृगया चोचिता राजन्नस्मिन्काले सुतस्य ते ।\nदुर्योधनस्य गमनं त्वमनुज्ञातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Hunting is also fitting at this season, king. You should give your son Duryodhana leave to go.'\""}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"मृगया शोभना तात गवां च समवेक्षणम् ।\nविश्रम्भस्तु न गन्तव्यो बल्लवानामिति स्मरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Hunting is fine, my dear, and so is looking over the cattle. But I recall that one should not place trust in the cowherds.'\""}},{"n":7,"text":"ते तु तत्र नरव्याघ्राः समीप इति नः श्रुतम् ।\nअतो नाभ्यनुजानामि गमनं तत्र वः स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I have heard that those tigers among men are close by. So I do not give permission for you yourselves to go there.'\""}},{"n":8,"text":"छद्मना निर्जितास्ते हि कर्शिताश्च महावने ।\nतपोनित्याश्च राधेय समर्थाश्च महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'They were defeated by a trick and wasted away in the great forest. They are constantly given to austerity, Radheya, and are capable great warriors.'\""}},{"n":9,"text":"धर्मराजो न संक्रुध्येद्भीमसेनस्त्वमर्षणः ।\nयज्ञसेनस्य दुहिता तेज एव तु केवलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Dharmaraja might not grow angry, but Bhimasena is quick to wrath, and the daughter of Yajnasena is pure fire.'\""}},{"n":10,"text":"यूयं चाप्यपराध्येयुर्दर्पमोहसमन्विताः ।\nततो विनिर्दहेयुस्ते तपसा हि समन्विताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You might do them wrong, filled with pride and confusion. Then, being endowed with austerity, they could burn you.'\""}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ वा सायुधा वीरा मन्युनाभिपरिप्लुताः ।\nसहिता बद्धनिस्त्रिंशा दहेयुः शस्त्रतेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Or those heroes, armed and flooded with anger, together with swords bound on, could burn you with the force of their weapons.'\""}},{"n":12,"text":"अथ यूयं बहुत्वात्तानारभध्वं कथंचन ।\nअनार्यं परमं तत्स्यादशक्यं तच्च मे मतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Or if you, being many, attack them somehow, that would be most ignoble, and I think impossible.'\""}},{"n":13,"text":"उषितो हि महाबाहुरिन्द्रलोके धनंजयः ।\nदिव्यान्यस्त्राण्यवाप्याथ ततः प्रत्यागतो वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Dhananjaya, mighty-armed, has dwelt in Indra's world and gained divine weapons, and then returned to the forest.'\""}},{"n":14,"text":"अकृतास्त्रेण पृथिवी जिता बीभत्सुना पुरा ।\nकिं पुनः स कृतास्त्रोऽद्य न हन्याद्वो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Bibhatsu conquered the earth in the past when he had not yet gained weapons. How much more could that great chariot-warrior, now skilled in weapons, not kill you?'\""}},{"n":15,"text":"अथ वा मद्वचः श्रुत्वा तत्र यत्ता भविष्यथ ।\nउद्विग्नवासो विश्रम्भाद्दुःखं तत्र भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Or if you listen to my words and are on guard there, living there uneasily out of trust will bring sorrow.'\""}},{"n":16,"text":"अथ वा सैनिकाः केचिदपकुर्युर्युधिष्ठिरे ।\nतदबुद्धिकृतं कर्म दोषमुत्पादयेच्च वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Or some soldiers might injure Yudhishthira, and that deed, done without your knowledge, might bring fault on you.'\""}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्माद्गच्छन्तु पुरुषाः स्मारणायाप्तकारिणः ।\nन स्वयं तत्र गमनं रोचये तव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'So let trustworthy men go for the counting. I do not like your going there yourself, Bharata.'\""}},{"text":"शकुनिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"धर्मज्ञः पाण्डवो ज्येष्ठः प्रतिज्ञातं च संसदि ।\nतेन द्वादश वर्षाणि वस्तव्यानीति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The eldest Pandava knows dharma and made a vow in the assembly that they must live twelve years.'\""}},{"n":19,"text":"अनुवृत्ताश्च ते सर्वे पाण्डवा धर्मचारिणः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरश्च कौन्तेयो न नः कोपं करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'All the Pandavas follow dharma and are obedient, and Yudhishthira, Kunti's son, will not show anger toward us.'\""}},{"n":20,"text":"मृगयां चैव नो गन्तुमिच्छा संवर्धते भृशम् ।\nस्मारणं च चिकीर्षामो न तु पाण्डवदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Our wish to go hunting grows strong, and we want to do the counting, not to see the Pandavas.'\""}},{"n":21,"text":"न चानार्यसमाचारः कश्चित्तत्र भविष्यति ।\nन च तत्र गमिष्यामो यत्र तेषां प्रतिश्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'No ignoble act will take place there, and we will not go to where their dwelling is.'\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"एवमुक्तः शकुनिना धृतराष्ट्रो जनेश्वरः ।\nदुर्योधनं सहामात्यमनुजज्ञे न कामतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So addressed by Shakuni, King Dhritarashtra gave Duryodhana and his ministers leave, though not willingly.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"अनुज्ञातस्तु गान्धारिः कर्णेन सहितस्तदा ।\nनिर्ययौ भरतश्रेष्ठो बलेन महता वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having received leave, Gandhari's son, best of the Bharatas, set out with Karna, surrounded by a great army.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"दुःशासनेन च तथा सौबलेन च देविना ।\nसंवृतो भ्रातृभिश्चान्यैः स्त्रीभिश्चापि सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He was surrounded by Duhshasana, by Saubala the gambler, by other brothers and by thousands of women.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"तं निर्यान्तं महाबाहुं द्रष्टुं द्वैतवनं सरः ।\nपौराश्चानुययुः सर्वे सहदारा वनं च तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As the mighty-armed one set out to see the lake Dvaitavana, the townspeople with their wives followed him to that forest.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"अष्टौ रथसहस्राणि त्रीणि नागायुतानि च ।\nपत्तयो बहुसाहस्रा हयाश्च नवतिः शताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There were eight thousand chariots, thirty thousand elephants, many thousands of foot-soldiers, and nine thousand horses.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"शकटापणवेश्याश्च वणिजो बन्दिनस्तथा ।\nनराश्च मृगयाशीलाः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There were carts, shops, courtesans, merchants, bards, and hundreds and thousands of men fond of hunting.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः प्रयाणे नृपतेः सुमहानभवत्स्वनः ।\nप्रावृषीव महावायोरुद्धतस्य विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As the king set off there was a very great noise, like a great storm wind in the rainy season, lord of the people.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"गव्यूतिमात्रे न्यवसद्राजा दुर्योधनस्तदा ।\nप्रयातो वाहनैः सर्वैस्ततो द्वैतवनं सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"King Duryodhana camped at a distance of a gavyuti, then went on with all his vehicles to the lake at Dvaitavana.\""}}]}]}